# Radxa NIO 12L — userpatches kernel config fragment
# Merged on top of config/kernel/linux-genio-edge.config by Armbian compile.sh.
#
# When updating the edge-genio kernel:
#   1. Run compile.sh (see docs/usb-audio.md in radxa-nio-12l repo for the full command)
#   2. This fragment is picked up automatically — no changes needed
#   3. Install the resulting linux-image-edge-genio_*.deb on the board
#   4. Re-run: sudo apt-mark hold linux-image-edge-genio
#
# Why this fragment exists:
#   CONFIG_SND_USB_AUDIO (ALSA USB audio host driver) was compiled out in the
#   Armbian-distributed 6.19.0-rc5-edge-genio image. USB audio devices are
#   enumerated by the kernel (lsusb shows them) but ALSA cannot attach to them.
#   This fragment enables it as a loadable module.
#
#   Note: CONFIG_USB_AUDIO (already in the base config) is the USB *gadget*
#   audio function — it makes the board appear as a USB audio device to a host.
#   That is unrelated to this fix.

CONFIG_SND_USB_AUDIO=m
